 "transcript": {
  "answer": "I can't give you an AUD-to-peso rate from my data. The Reserve Bank of Australia doesn't publish one for the Argentine peso, and none of my sources include it.\n\nYou can work it out yourself using the US dollar. As of 16 October 2026, A$1 bought US$0.6947 (RBA, 4pm AEST). Multiply that by the current number of pesos per US dollar:\n\n**Pesos per A$1 ≈ 0.6947 × (pesos per US$1)**\n\nFor example, if US$1 buys 1,400 pesos, A$1 buys about 973 pesos (0.6947 × 1,400).\n\nArgentina has had several exchange rates at once, such as the official rate and the parallel \"blue\" rate, and they can be far apart. For the peso side, use whichever rate fits what you're doing: the Banco Central de la República Argentina for the official rate, or a money changer or card provider for what you'll actually get. Banks and card issuers will also add their own margin.",
